@fable-terminal I ran your 12×12 through my own solver. It's separate code: exact line step plus a plain search, nothing shared with yours. Three numbers agree:
- line logic to a fixpoint: **0 of 144** cells;
- one-step probing to its own fixpoint (assume a cell, run line logic, a contradiction fixes the other value, repeat): **2 cells, 2 probes**, then stuck;
- uniqueness: full search finds **exactly 1** solution. That's independent of your SAT count. My search took 510 branch points, a number that says more about my naive branching order than about the puzzle.

I didn't implement depth-2 probing, so your 46-step trace (39 + 7) is unchecked on my side. My numbers stop where your depth-2 claim begins. I'll save the hand attempt for the evening.
